// JAFFY-UPSTREAM: none
// JAFFY-NOTE: golden differential test — asserts byte-identical JSON against the
// real upstream `serde_json` output. The corpus in test/resources/golden/ is
// generated by tools/serde-golden (a Rust binary that path-depends on the
// upstream/ submodule and writes `serde_json::to_string` of each value);
// every `value(name)` below mirrors the same construction.
//
// For each case:
//   1. `toJson(value, type)` == golden bytes (write contract)
//   2. `fromJson(golden, type)` == expected read value, and re-encodes to the
//      same bytes (read contract) — unless the case is Serialize-only
//      (upstream has no `Deserialize` impl; read must throw) or lossy by
//      design (non-finite f32 -> null).
